ially capture the most frequent relationship betweent them are\n- **Dependency Parsing** capture the relations based on what we see in the text\n\nThey could complement each other","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### Bootstrapping\n\nThe general idea of bootstrapping is like a `GREP`, we match the strings that have our concepts, then we see what's between them, relationships will emerge as more common they are.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"from collections import Counter\nimport re\n\ndef get_text_between(sentence, concept_a, concept_b):\n    pattern = rf'{re.escape(concept_a)}(.+?){re.escape(concept_b)}'\n    match = re.search(pattern, sentence.lower())\n    if match:\n        return match.group(1).strip()\n    return None\n\ndef bootstrap_relations(sentence, concept_map, top_k=20, min_count=2):\n    top_concepts = [c for c, _ in sorted(\n        concept_map.items(),\n        key=lambda x: x[1]['count'],\n        reverse=True\n    )[:top_k]]\n\n    between_patterns = Counter()\n    relation_examples = {}\n\n    for sentence in sentences:\n        text = sentence['text'].lower()\n\n        for i, concept_a in enumerate(top_concepts):\n            for concept_b in top_concepts[i+1:]:\n                if concept_a not in text or concept_b not in text:\n                    continue\n\n                between = get_text_between(text, concept_a, concept_b)\n                if not between:\n                    between = get_text_between(text, concept_b, concept_a)\n                    if between:\n                        concept_a, concept_b = concept_b, concept_a\n\n                if between and 2 < len(between.split()) < 4:\n                    between_patterns[between] += 1\n\n                    if between not in relation_examples:\n                        relation_examples[between] = []\n                    if len(relation_examples[between]) < 3:\n                        relation_examples[between].append(f'({concept_a}) [{between}] ({concept_b})')\n\n    print('Most frequent patterns between concepts:\\n')\n    for pattern, count in between_patterns.most_common(20):\n        if count >= min_count:\n            print(f\" '{pattern}' -> count: {count}\")\n            for ex in relation_examples[pattern]:\n                print(f\"    e.g. {ex}\")\n            print()\n            \n    return between_patterns, relation_examples","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-06-04T14:10:23.028532Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-06-04T14:10:23.029217Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-06-04T14:10:23.037451Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-06-04T14:10:23.029188Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-06-04T14:10:23.036522Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":19},{"cell_type":"code","source":"patterns, examples = bootstrap_relations(sentences, concepts_nc, top_k=20, min_count=2)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-06-04T14:10:31.209856Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-06-04T14:10:31.210285Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-06-04T14:10:31.237728Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-06-04T14:10:31.210239Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-06-04T14:10:31.236776Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Most frequent patterns between concepts:\n\n 's for a' -> count: 3\n    e.g. (voltage) [s for a] (digit)\n    e.g. (voltage) [s for a] (digital circuit)\n    e.g. (voltage) [s for a] (digital circuit)\n\n 'provides an analog' -> count: 2\n    e.g. (sensor) [provides an analog] (voltage)\n    e.g. (sensor) [provides an analog] (voltage)\n\n 'procedure for combinational' -> count: 2\n    e.g. (design) [procedure for combinational] (digit)\n    e.g. (design) [procedure for combinational] (digital circuit)\n\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":21},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"As we store the lemmas of our concepts we run into problems when we came across plurales of modified words of them, in this example \n> voltage -> voltages\n\nSo instead of capturing *for a* as a relationship we capture *s for a* as the lemma doesn't have that s, also in the other end we have repetition for the same stuff, digit and digital circuits it's a by product of matching the lemma of a single and compound concept","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"def get_concept_pattern(concept):\n    base = re.escape(concept)\n    # Match base form + optional s, es, ed, ing\n    return rf'\\b{base}(?:s|es|ed|ing)?\\b'\n\ndef get_text_between(sentence, concept_a, concept_b):\n    pattern_a = get_concept_pattern(concept_a)\n    pattern_b = get_concept_pattern(concept_b)\n    \n    pattern = rf'({pattern_a})(.+?)({pattern_b})'\n    match = re.search(pattern, sentence.lower())\n    if match:\n        return match.group(2).strip()  # group 2 = between\n    return None","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-06-04T14:10:38.326983Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-06-04T14:10:38.327319Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-06-04T14:10:38.332837Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-06-04T14:10:38.327292Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-06-04T14:10:38.332086Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":22},{"cell_type":"code","source":"patterns, examples = bootstrap_relations(sentences, concepts_nc, top_k=20, min_count=2)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-06-04T14:10:44.427353Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-06-04T14:10:44.428087Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-06-04T14:10:44.478902Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-06-04T14:10:44.428053Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-06-04T14:10:44.478225Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Most frequent patterns between concepts:\n\n 'provides an analog' -> count: 2\n    e.g. (sensor) [provides an analog] (voltage)\n    e.g. (sensor) [provides an analog] (voltage)\n\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":23},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"Even though we fix it we can't use really the core of bootstrapping as frequencies in one chapter of a notebook that we are using is limited, making pat